    "created_at": "2019-12-01T13:56:01Z",
    "updated_at": "2019-12-01T13:56:01Z",
    "body": "As it turns out, starship tries to look for the `PWD` environment variable before falling back to `env::current_dir()`. When you run Powershell from some Unix shell such as bash, the `PWD` stays in the directory in which bash executed Powershell. Since Powershell does not set this variable, the directory in Starship seems \"stuck\"",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
